{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And I shall separate you from the peoples to be Mine.</b> The wisdom of the Torah obligated us to be separated in our eating, in our drinking, and in our attire; and because we are disposed toward the commandments of the Torah, they are jealous of us, and through their jealousy they hate us — as the Sages, whose memory is for a blessing, expounded: 'Har Chorev is its name; and why was it called Sinai? Because from there hatred came forth upon the worshippers of idols.'" "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״ואבדיל אתכם מן העמים להיות לי״ — 'If you are separated from the idolaters, then you are Mine; and if not, then you belong to Nebuchadnezzar and his companions.' Rabbi Elazar ben Azariah said: From where do we learn that a person should not say, 'I have no desire to wear kilayim (mixed species), and I have no desire to come upon forbidden relations, I have no desire to eat the flesh of a pig' — but rather, 'I desire it, and what shall I do, for my Father in heaven has decreed it upon me'? Scripture says: ״ואבדיל אתכם מן העמים להיות לי״ — that your separation from them should be for the sake of Heaven, and thus one is found to withdraw from transgression and to accept upon himself the yoke of the kingdom of Heaven.<br> And the fact that it used the term <b>the peoples</b> (העמים) is as if it said 'dark ones' (חשכים); the Targum renders כהה (Leviticus 13) as עמיא, for the nations have dimmed their eyes from seeing the light of the Torah because they have no Torah, and they walk in the ways of darkness — as it is written (Isaiah 29:15): ״והיה במחשך מעשיהם״, and they are destined for Gehenna, which is called darkness, as it is said (Job 20:26): ״כל חשך טמון לצפוניו״, and it is written (I Samuel): ״ורשעים בחשך ידמו״. But Israel merit the hidden light stored away for the righteous in the world to come, in the merit of their having received the Torah, which is called light, as it is said (Psalms 119:105): ״נר לרגלי דברך ואור לנתיבתי״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {1 "The Aramaic Targum rendering of כהה as עמיא is taken from Onkelos on Leviticus 13:39; the wordplay linking עמים and חשכים rests on this Targumic equation. The citation '(שמואל א)' is given without verse number; 'ורשעים בחשך ידמו' is from I Samuel 2:9."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:32.911526247Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}